WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.570
- [Narrator] This is Elsie.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.570
She's a Komodo dragon...

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.178
The largest species of
lizard on Earth today.

00:00:08.178 --> 00:00:10.761
(gentle music)

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.383
Females like Elsie can
grow to be 6 feet long

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.740
and males are known to
reach 10 feet and weigh over

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.810
200 pounds.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.280
They are fierce hunters and
can incapacitate large prey

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.590
like deer, water buffalo,
and on rare occasions,

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.310
human beings.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:34.610
Its bacterial-laced
saliva often causes fatal

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.490
blood poisoning within 24 hours.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.230
The Komodo dragon can consume
up to 80% of its body weight

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.950
in a single feeding.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.790
Native to five Indonesian islands,

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:48.580
Komodo dragons are territorial
and spend much of their

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.867
time alone.

00:00:49.867 --> 00:00:53.970
These fearsome predators
face numerous threats.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.880
Earthquakes, volcanic
activity, habitat loss,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.407
and illegal poaching have
reduced the wild populations

00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:02.070
to only a few thousand.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:07.043
This is the Komodo dragon.
(gentle music)

